It comes from `{{ location }}` in the repository configuration.
{%- if pattern != glob %}

There it is written as `{{ pattern }}`, which expands to `{{ glob }}`.
{%- endif %}

Parsing failed with the error:

```
{{ error }}
```

## What to do?

Characters other than `0-9`, `A-Z`, `a-z`, `_`, `-`, `.`, and ` ` must be escaped with `\`.  For example, the glob `prod/@vars/*.tf` must be written `prod/\@vars/*.tf`.

A `**` is allowed only next to a `/`, so `**/*` and `modules/**` are valid but `**` on its own is not.

If you are using `${DIR}` or `${WORKSPACE}`, they must be written with the `{` and `}`.

See the [documentation](https://stategraph.com/docs/reference/orchestration/configuration/when-modified#keys) for file globs.
